// big-rusty-drums — an SFZ kit of k7-rack: Karoryfer's Big Rusty Drums, an old 22" kick and toms, a 14" snare, hi-hat,
// a ride and a crash with sizzles, and a china, with stick, brush and mallet articulations. CC0, so it is free of any
// condition. Played by the engine's own SFZ player (sfizz), one ENGINE of k7-rack: a tap per piece.
//
// Close to General MIDI: kick 36 (undamped 35), side-stick 37, snare 38 (edge 39, rimshot 40), toms 41 43 45 47 from
// the 22" floor up, hi-hat 42 (closed) 44 (pedal) 46 (open), ride 51 (crash 52, bell 53), crash 49, china 57. Its
// other notes are chokes, brush stirs and the like, played but not drawn. The samples (~620 MB) are not in the
// library: the engine's machine keeps them, its supervisor fetching them once chosen in the tray's Downloads tab.
extends("@engine/sfz-player")
params({
  sfz: "@instruments/big-rusty-drums/Programs/01-full.sfz",
  // Its loudest hit at full velocity, the kick, peaks at 0 dBFS — the level a rack's normalised samples play at.
  Volume: 6.4,
})
// The pads its panel draws, on the notes the kit plays them on.
kit({
  KickOpen: 35,
  Kick: 36,
  SideStick: 37,
  Snare: 38,
  SnareEdge: 39,
  Rimshot: 40,
  Tom22: 41,
  HatClosed: 42,
  Tom18: 43,
  HatPedal: 44,
  Tom15: 45,
  HatOpen: 46,
  Tom14: 47,
  Crash: 49,
  RideBow: 51,
  RideCrash: 52,
  RideBell: 53,
  HatShank: 54,
  HatSplash: 56,
  China: 57,
})
// A real acoustic drum kit with brushes and mallets, rusty and characterful — Big Rusty Drums by Karoryfer (CC0). Its samples, about 620 MB, download from the k7 tray's Downloads tab.
